/* ============================================================
   VR LAYER v3 (Quest 3 and any WebXR headset) · Oct 2026
   Same file for allofus.one (aou-xr.js) and worldvrmall.com (wvm-xr.js); only the four module names at the top differ (wvm-engine, wvm-go, wvm-icons, wvm-lifevr). Generated from aou-xr.js on Oct 19 2026: copy this file to the mall repo as js/wvm-xr.js.
   v3 (Oct 8 2026):
   - Menu is world-locked by default (it stays where you open it; "📌 Menu" under Me pins it to your view instead) and is
     tabbed: 🧭 Go (every place, paged) · 🌍 Worlds (every site in the network + inside/outside) · 🧍 Me · 🛠️ Help. Curved, narrower, no squinting.
   - Laser comes out of the index fingertip of the robot hand (toggle under Me). Trigger on open ground = go there.
   - First person: your body stands under your head (lean, step, walk the room: it follows), so looking down shows your own body.
   - Speed: no scene walk per frame (signs are listed every 3 s), button faces cached, raycast every 3rd frame, shadows frozen
     instead of switched off (no shader recompiles on entry / exit), the laser works with one controller.
   - Floor: if the headset's origin lands at eye level (the "feet of a giant" view) it is detected within a
     second and corrected; Raise / Lower / Reset view live in the menu.
   - Views: X cycles 1st person → follow cam (3 m behind, your whole body in front of you) → drone (9 m up).
   - Size: hold BOTH grips and pull the controllers apart / together = you grow (giant) or shrink (ant). Menu has
     Bigger / Smaller / Life-size. Rides and vehicles always reset you to life-size first.
   - Laser (right hand): a glowing beam with a reticle. Trigger = click what it points at (signs, products, ride
     pads, menu buttons). Grip while pointing = GRAB: you are pulled to that spot (up to 60 m, obstacle-checked).
     Right stick click = teleport to the ground spot. Store / website buttons leave VR cleanly and open the site.
   - Move: left stick walks where you look. Turn: right stick snaps 30° (menu can switch to smooth turn).
   - Menu: Y (or the wrist button) opens a big floating panel in front of your face: places, rides, views,
     size, floor, turn mode, bug report, exit. Point and pull the trigger.
   - Smooth: every lazy zone is built behind the dark intro (no hitches while walking), shaders are precompiled,
     draw distance and fog are tightened while presenting, 0.9 framebuffer scale + foveation, no per-frame
     allocations in the poll.
   - B = bug report with your position (form opens when you leave VR). A = do the nearest thing.
   ============================================================ */
